<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Persetel yr EPS up 52 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Persetel yr EPS up 52 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended May 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		70.1	  vs 46.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 25.7	  vs 19.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings between 68.0 and 70.0 cents a share with consensus at 69.3 cents. They expected a dividend of between 27.0 and 28.0 cents, averaging out at 27.6.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   158.3	 vs 77.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   166.6	 vs 75.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 25.9	  vs 12.6</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   27.0	  vs 19.8</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,666.3     vs 1,079.4</p>
<p>Div payable Sept 25</p>
<p>on register Aug 22</p>
<p>Full name: Persetel Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
